    {
      "claim_id": "hardware-bus-chipset",
      "verdict": "supported",
      "targets": [
        {
          "source_id": "web-computer-science-computer-hardware",
          "evidence_id": "evidence-06bce453287a"
        }
      ],
      "supporting_quotes": [
        {
          "evidence_id": "evidence-06bce453287a",
          "exact": "The internal bus connects the CPU to main memory via multiple communication lines—typically 50 to 100—divided into address, data, and control buses, each handling specific types of signals. Historically, parallel buses were dominant, but in the twenty-first century, high-speed serial buses (often using serializer/deserializer (SerDes) technology) have largely replaced them, enabling greater data throughput over fewer physical connections. Examples include PCI Express and USB. In systems with multiple processors, an interconnect bus is used, traditionally coordinated by a northbridge chip, which links the CPU, memory, and high-speed peripherals such as PCI. The southbridge handles communication with slower I/O devices such as storage."
        }
      ],
      "observations": [
        {
          "evidence_id": "evidence-06bce453287a",
          "subject": "internal bus (divided into address, data, and control buses; superseded by high-speed serial buses such as PCI Express and USB; multi-processor systems coordinated by northbridge/southbridge)",
          "predicate": "connects",
          "object": "CPU to main memory; northbridge links CPU, memory and high-speed peripherals (e.g., PCI), southbridge handles slower I/O devices (e.g., storage)",
          "qualifiers": {
            "origin": "external",
            "confidentiality": "public",
            "evidence_status": "source-reported"
          }
        }
      ],
      "applied_rule_refs": [
        "EVD-001",
        "VAL-001",
        "VAL-002"
      ],
      "rationale": "引文区间 [0,743) 三部分与 claim 逐一对应：'connects the CPU to main memory via multiple communication lines ... divided into address, data, and control buses' 对应 '内部总线用地址、数据、控制等多条通信线连接 CPU 与主存'；'in the twenty-first century, high-speed serial buses ... Examples include PCI Express and USB' 对应 '21 世纪高速串行总线（如 PCI Express、USB）取代了并行总线'；'traditionally coordinated by a northbridge chip, which links the CPU, memory, and high-speed peripherals such as PCI. The southbridge handles communication with slower I/O devices such as storage' 对应 '北桥协调 CPU、内存与高速外设，南桥负责较慢的 I/O 设备'。映射完整（含 '历史上并行总线占主导' 与 '取代' 语义），无增删与冲突，判 supported。",
      "rationale_offsets": [
